{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VoPAAJvKvYNjDWdV719bG9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","number":3402,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) O3-5741: Resolve stale conditions cache on visit note diagnosis addition","state":"closed","author":"Abhishek-IITP","createdAt":"2026-06-18T12:49:54.000Z","mergedAt":null,"closedAt":"2026-06-18T15:04:32.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart/pull/3402","mergeCommit":null,"syncedAt":"2026-10-23T19:00:04.598Z","tickets":[{"key":"O3-5741","source":"ticket-pattern"}],"commits":[],"files":[{"path":"packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.test.ts","additions":36,"deletions":4},{"path":"packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts","additions":18,"deletions":1}],"body":"## Requirements\r\n- [ ] Tests\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nThis PR fixes a stale cache issue in the Conditions workspace.\r\n\r\nPreviously, when a diagnosis was added through the Visit Note workspace and the user navigated to the Conditions tab in the patient chart, the newly created condition did not appear immediately. Users had to manually refresh the browser page before the condition became visible.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Root Cause**\r\n\r\nThe Conditions workspace was displaying cached data and was not revalidating condition data after a diagnosis was created from a Visit Note.\r\n\r\n**Solution :**\r\n- Added cache invalidation/revalidation after diagnosis creation.\r\n- Ensured the Conditions list fetches the latest patient condition data when navigating from Visit Note to the Conditions tab.\r\n- Removed the requirement for a manual browser refresh to see newly added conditions.\r\n\r\n## Demo Video\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1gtREblhaiyKSDr-NnTb5uZLa4IrNQcr5/view?usp=sharing\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\nO3-5741\r\n\r\n","comments":[{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-06-18T15:04:32.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"Thanks @Abhishek-IITP! But, as discussed in [this](https://talk.openmrs.org/t/why-do-we-display-diagnoses-in-the-conditions-list/49608/4) talk post, we don’t actually need to show diagnoses in the conditions table, so closing this for now. We do appreciate you work and interest though so please do feel free to work on a different issue. Thanks again!"},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"Abhishek-IITP","createdAt":"2026-06-18T15:30:17.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"@NethmiRodrigo please go through [this link](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5741) , i did what mentioned here."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-06-19T08:31:53.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"> @NethmiRodrigo please go through [this link](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5741) , i did what mentioned here.\r\n\r\nYes, but as per the discussion on the talk post I’ve linked, the behaviour itself has changed, so that ticket itself should be corrected."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"Abhishek-IITP","createdAt":"2026-06-19T08:53:47.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"Thanks for the clarification. I understand now that the product decision has changed and diagnoses will no longer be displayed in the Conditions table. The original ticket led me to investigate the stale cache issue, but I understand why the fix is no longer needed. I'll look for another issue to contribute to. Thanks! @NethmiRodrigo "}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd3d322b-0274-448d-9e81-23b7ccd3fa9d","uuid":"5f440bc5-f15e-430c-8f3d-20aac43a139a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:00:56.384Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","number":3402,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) O3-5741: Resolve stale conditions cache on visit note diagnosis addition","state":"closed","author":"Abhis