 please do feel free to work on a different issue. Thanks again!"},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"Abhishek-IITP","createdAt":"2026-06-18T15:30:17.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"@NethmiRodrigo please go through [this link](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5741) , i did what mentioned here."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-06-19T08:31:53.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"> @NethmiRodrigo please go through [this link](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5741) , i did what mentioned here.\r\n\r\nYes, but as per the discussion on the talk post I’ve linked, the behaviour itself has changed, so that ticket itself should be corrected."},{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"Abhishek-IITP","createdAt":"2026-06-19T08:53:47.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"Thanks for the clarification. I understand now that the product decision has changed and diagnoses will no longer be displayed in the Conditions table. The original ticket led me to investigate the stale cache issue, but I understand why the fix is no longer needed. I'll look for another issue to contribute to. Thanks! @NethmiRodrigo "}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VoPAAJvKvYNjDWdV719bG9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
